# Trail record

One entry of a problem's trail, the hash-chained memory every attempt reads
first. Each `hash` is the SHA-256 of the previous hash and the entry's canonical
body, so changing, dropping or reordering an entry breaks the chain from there.
Genesis is sixty-four zeros, as the coordinator's schema enforces.

## A TrailEntry has:
    a seq, which is Int.
    a ts, which is Int.
    a problemId, which is Text.
    a stage, which is Text.
    a kind, which is Text.
    a contributor, which is Text.
    a model, which is Text.
    a strategyId, which is Text.
    a promptSha, which is Text.
    an approachFingerprint, which is Text.
    an artifactShas, which is Seq of Text.
    a verdict, which is Text.
    an exitCode, which is Int.
    a diagnostics, which is Text.
    a costMicros, which is Int.
    a summary, which is Text.
    a nextSuggestions, which is Seq of Text.
    a prevHash, which is Text.
    a hash, which is Text.

## Note
The canonical body: every field but the hashes, in order, with `json.lg`'s
canonical escaping — written out so the chain never changes with the encoder.

## To canonicalTrailBody (e: TrailEntry) -> Text:
    Let mutable parts be ["\"seq\":{e's seq}", "\"ts\":{e's ts}", "\"problemId\":" + jsonQuote(e's problemId), "\"stage\":" + jsonQuote(e's stage)].
    Push "\"kind\":" + jsonQuote(e's kind) + ",\"contributor\":" + jsonQuote(e's contributor) + ",\"model\":" + jsonQuote(e's model) to parts.
    Push "\"strategyId\":" + jsonQuote(e's strategyId) + ",\"promptSha\":" + jsonQuote(e's promptSha) to parts.
    Push "\"approachFingerprint\":" + jsonQuote(e's approachFingerprint) + ",\"artifactShas\":" + jsonSerialize(textArray(e's artifactShas)) to parts.
    Push "\"verdict\":" + jsonQuote(e's verdict) + ",\"exitCode\":{e's exitCode},\"diagnostics\":" + jsonQuote(e's diagnostics) to parts.
    Push "\"costMicros\":{e's costMicros},\"summary\":" + jsonQuote(e's summary) to parts.
    Push "\"nextSuggestions\":" + jsonSerialize(textArray(e's nextSuggestions)) to parts.
    Return "{{" + join(parts, ",") + "}}".

## To textArray (xs: Seq of Text) -> Json:
    Let mutable elems be a new Seq of Json.
    Repeat for x in xs:
        Push (a new JStr with s x) to elems.
    Return a new JArr with elems elems.

## To trailHash (prevHash: Text, e: TrailEntry) -> Text:
    Return bytesToHex(sha256(text_bytes(prevHash + canonicalTrailBody(e)))).

## To sealEntry (e: TrailEntry, seq: Int, prevHash: Text) -> TrailEntry:
    Let mutable out be e.
    Set out's seq to seq.
    Set out's prevHash to prevHash.
    Set out's hash to trailHash(prevHash, out).
    Return out.

## Note
The trail with `e` sealed onto its end: the trail numbers and chains it.

## To appendToTrail (trail: Seq of TrailEntry, e: TrailEntry) -> Seq of TrailEntry:
    Let mutable prev be repeatText("0", 64).
    If length of trail is greater than 0:
        Set prev to (item (length of trail) of trail)'s hash.
    Let mutable out be copy of trail.
    Push sealEntry(e, length of trail + 1, prev) to out.
    Return out.

## Note
The first broken link, or the empty text when every link holds.

## To verifyTrail (trail: Seq of TrailEntry) -> Text:
    Let mutable prev be repeatText("0", 64).
    Let mutable i be 0.
    Repeat for e in trail:
        Set i to i + 1.
        If e's seq is not equal to i:
            Return "entry {i}: seq is {e's seq}, expected {i}".
        If e's problemId is not equal to (item 1 of trail)'s problemId:
            Return "entry {i}: belongs to {e's problemId}".
        If e's prevHash is not equal to prev or e's hash is not equal to trailHash(prev, e):
            Return "entry {i}: does not chain from entry {i - 1}".
        Set prev to e's hash.
    Return "".

## Note
An entry with the fields every attempt has and the rest empty.

## To blankEntry (problemId: Text, kind: Text, verdict: Text, diagnostics: Text) -> TrailEntry:
    Let mutable e be a new TrailEntry with seq 0 and ts 0 and problemId problemId and stage "in_progress" and kind kind and verdict verdict.
    Set e's diagnostics to diagnostics.
    Return e.

## Test: the canonical body is valid JSON that names no hash

Let mutable e be blankEntry("opdp:116", "prove", "rejected", "block 3: `rfl` \"x\"\n").
Set e's artifactShas to ["d1", "d2"].
Expect that jsonValid(canonicalTrailBody(e)) is equal to true.
Expect that canonicalTrailBody(e) contains "\"artifactShas\":[\"d1\",\"d2\"]".
Expect that jsonHas(jsonParse(canonicalTrailBody(e)), "prevHash") is equal to false.

## Test: appending chains entries and editing one breaks the chain there

Let mutable t be appendToTrail(appendToTrail([], blankEntry("p", "prove", "rejected", "x")), blankEntry("p", "repair", "verified", "")).
Expect that verifyTrail(t) is equal to "" and (item 2 of t)'s prevHash is equal to (item 1 of t)'s hash.
Set item 1 of t to blankEntry("p", "prove", "verified", "x").
Expect that verifyTrail(t) is equal to "entry 1: seq is 0, expected 1".

## Test: a sealed entry edited in any field no longer chains

For all booleans tamper:
    Let mutable t be appendToTrail([], blankEntry("p", "prove", "rejected", "block 4: x")).
    Let mutable e be item 1 of t.
    If tamper:
        Set e's diagnostics to "it worked, honest".
    Set item 1 of t to e.
    Let holds be verifyTrail(t) is equal to "".
    Expect that holds is equal to (not tamper).
